      "text": [
        " «لاَ» قِيلَ فَالصَّائِمُ قَالَ «لاَ» قِيلَ يَشَمُّ اَلصَّائِمُ اَلْغَالِيَةَ وَ اَلدُّخْنَةَ قَالَ «نَعَمْ» قِيلَ كَيْفَ حَلَّ لَهُ أَنْ يَشَمَّ اَلطِّيبَ وَ لاَ يَشَمَّ اَلرَّيْحَانَ قَالَ «لِأَنَّ اَلطِّيبَ سُنَّةٌ وَ اَلرَّيْحَانَ بِدْعَةٌ لِلصَّائِمِ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1879 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) was asked about a person in a state of Ihram smelling basil. Imam (as) said: \"No.\"\nImam (as) was asked about a fasting person. Imam (as) said: \"No.\"\nImam (as) was asked if a fasting person may smell perfume or incense. Imam (as) said: \"Yes.\"\nImam (as) was asked: \"How is it permissible for him to smell perfume but not basil?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"Because perfume is a Sunnah, while basil is an innovation for the fasting person.\""
        ]
      }
